<div class="container">
    <h1 class="doc-h1">Changelog 2026-08-19 — AI Agent Orchestration + Notification Recovery</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" doc-muted>
        Last Updated: 2026-08-19 | Version: 0.1 | Tracked in project:
        <a href="/project/details?project_id=267" class="doc-link">#267 (AGENTS)</a>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">What changed</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>New plan <a href="/Documentation/AIAgentOrchestrationPlan" class="doc-link">AIAgentOrchestrationPlan</a></strong> (proj #267 AGENTS, sub-project of the Autonomous Agents plan). Defines: (a) the two agent classes — branch-context <code>.hermes.md</code> files (done, focused) vs specialized recurring agents; (b) operational agents (Email agent = missing input; Secretary agent = DB-eval &#8594; VoIP critical call, text/voice/browser, multi-model Ollama/OpenRouter/Grok); (c) in-app agents (HelpDesk/Beekeeping/Ency) blocked until their todos exist; (d) principles + phasing + project tracking.</li>
                <li><strong>Notification regression recorded.</strong> Historically in-app + system + email worked; today ONLY email works. Logged as a separate blocking todo (not folded into agent work).</li>
                <li><strong>VoIP config page planned.</strong> Successor to the old Perl4 "call a page" feature — a new page where the user registers their own VoIP number so the Secretary can call them. You confirmed the old Perl4 app had this pattern.</li>
                <li><strong>Cross-links added.</strong> MASTER_PLAN Planning nav + reference list now link the new plan; AutonomousAgentsPlan (parent #267) gained a "Child plan" link. Plan's See Also links back to both.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="doc-h2">Open item (not done this session)</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>The SECRETARY-AGENT sub-project under #267 was NOT created via the API — <code>POST /api/projects</code> returned 200 but did not persist (count stayed 250). Create it in the app project UI, then stamp its ID into plan &#167;6. The plan references it as "SECRETARY-AGENT, child of #267" until then.</li>
            </ul>

